node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local
.vite/
coverage/

# Design mockups embed base64 fonts (~320KB each) — local-only comps, not code
design/*.html

# Real calendar data: personal schedules, other people's names, appointments.
# This repo is public. Generated .ics files stay on the machine that made them.
design/import/
*.ics

# Python (segmentation tooling)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Mockups copied into public/ only so the dev server can serve them. public/ is
# published from Pages, and a working mockup is not something to publish — the
# committed copy lives in design/ (HANDOFF, "public/ holds only what the app ships").
public/*-mockups.html
public/*-viewer.html

# Claude Code's working directory. Untracked is right — settings.local.json and
# the agent worktrees are per-machine — but NOT ignoring it is expensive:
# `.claude/worktrees/` holds full checkouts, each with its own node_modules, so
# every `git ls-files --others` walks them. Two of those wedged at 2.7 GB apiece
# on 2026-09-07 and took the machine to 0.7 GB free, which killed the dev server.
.claude/
